BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Turtle Feeding\, McCormick's Creek State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260927T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260927T110000
UID:7f087399e5f9ca1691bc8a58057fb576@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Come see our local Red-eared Slider hunt for fish. This progra
 m is held at the Canyon Inn.&nbsp\;&nbsp\; Nature Center is open every day
  from 10 am-5 pm EDT in May-October Closed on Tuesdays and Wendesdays Nove
 mber-April Upcoming programs can be seen by visiting on.in.gov/mccormicksc
 reek Our interpretive programs are designed to entertain and enrich folks 
 of all ages. Children under 12 must have an adult with them at the program
 s. Registration is not required for programs (unless stated). All our prog
 rams are free (unless otherwise noted). They are open to the public after 
 paying the park entrance fee. All our Interpretive programs are listed in 
 Eastern Daylight Savings Time. *Note that during peak visitation times\, e
 ntry into our park might be delayed. The drive to the Nature Center can ta
 ke 8 minutes. Please plan accordingly.&nbsp\; If you need more information
 \, call 812-829-2235 ext. 2
LOCATION:McCormick's Creek State Park\, Canyon Inn Lobby\, 250 McCormick's
  Creek Park Road\, Spencer\, IN 47460
URL:https://on.in.gov/mccormickscreek
X-SOURCE:McCormick's Creek State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cold Blooded Buffet\, McCormick's Creek State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260927T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260927T143000
UID:524032cbbdf05f558b885783f53dfe4e@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Hop and slither to the Nature Center to see our resident repti
 les chow down on bugs and mice. Learn cool facts about Indiana&#39\;s nati
 ve amphibians and reptiles.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\; Nature Center is open eve
 ry day from 9:30 am-5 pm EDT May-October. Closed on Tuesdays &amp\; Wednes
 days November-April Upcoming programs can be seen by visiting on.in.gov/mc
 cormickscreek Our interpretive programs are designed to entertain and enri
 ch folks of all ages. Children under 12 must have an adult with them at th
 e programs. Registration is not required for programs (unless stated). All
  our programs are free (unless otherwise noted). They are open to the publ
 ic after paying the park entrance fee. All our Interpretive programs are l
 isted in Eastern Daylight Savings Time. *Note that during peak visitation 
 times\, entry into our park might be delayed. The drive to the Nature Cent
 er can take 8 minutes. Please plan accordingly. If you need more informati
 on\, call 812-829-2235 ext. 2
LOCATION:McCormick's Creek State Park\, Nature Center\, 250 McCormick's Cr
 eek Park Road\, Spencer\, IN 47460
URL:https://on.in.gov/mccormickscreek
X-SOURCE:McCormick's Creek State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Turtle Trot\, McCormick's Creek State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260927T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260927T163000
UID:ec8e81db4d51ef94357442496340e42a@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:(Live Animals) Did you know that Red Eared Sliders have a life
  span of 30 years? These are the most common turtles taken out of the wild
 . Know your facts before getting a turtle! Come meet some of our animal am
 bassadors at the Canyon Inn front lawn and learn why they don&rsquo\;t mak
 e great pets.
LOCATION:McCormick's Creek State Park\, Canyon Inn\, 250 McCormick's Creek
  Park Road\, Spencer\, IN 47460
URL:on.IN.gov/mccormickscreek
X-SOURCE:McCormick's Creek State Park
END:VEVENT
